{# Renders a per-session response-length directive when the user has #}
{# explicitly chosen "concise" or "detailed". "normal" / unset emits #}
{# nothing so the model uses its default discipline. #}
{% if response_length == "concise" %}
## Response length

Keep this answer short. Default to 1–3 sentences or a small bullet list.
Skip headings, preamble, and restating the question. Lead with the answer
itself; add a single follow-up sentence only if the answer is genuinely
ambiguous without it.
{% elif response_length == "detailed" %}
## Response length

Give a thorough answer. Use headings or numbered sections when the topic
has more than one part, walk through reasoning where it adds value, and
include the concrete data, caveats, and edge cases the user would
otherwise have to ask about. Do not pad — verbosity must come from real
content, not filler.
{% endif %}
